#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064038 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "73216188-6524-55c3-b945-86d13ef64170" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Trigonometric Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2bb17470-6365-5e08-b649-f9f42146a4c6" :question/math-academy-id "e-732" :question/problem "Calculate $f'(x)$ if $f(x) = 2\\sin (3x - 1)$." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function\n\n$$\nf = 2\\sin u, \\qquad u=3x-1\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d f}{\\textrm d u} = 2\\cos u, \\qquad\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = 3\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{df}{dx} &= \\frac{df}{du} \\cdot \\frac{du}{dx} \\\\\n&= 2\\cos u \\cdot 3 \\\\\n&= 6\\cos u \\\\\n&= 6\\cos (3x - 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064039 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8ef81a0d-5a3a-5d7c-83e9-7d9ed0e8c5c6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Reciprocal Trigonometric Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7f56b401-c800-5708-8978-b84ce3f542f5" :question/math-academy-id "e-733" :question/problem "Calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x}$ if $y = 4\\csc (5x + 3)$." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny = 4 \\csc u, \\qquad u = 5x+3\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d u} = -4\\csc u\\cot u, \\qquad\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = 5\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{dy}{du} \\cdot \\frac{du}{dx} \\\\\n&=-4\\csc u\\cot u \\cdot 5 \\\\\n&=-20\\csc u\\cot u \\\\\n&=-20\\csc (5x + 3)\\cot (5x + 3)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064040 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ec11481-cea2-514b-aa78-707fcf8838cc" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Power of a Trigonometric Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "373a63fc-3dae-5880-8a49-63b5c64888f3" :question/math-academy-id "e-734" :question/problem "Given that $f(x) = \\sin^3{x}$, calculate $f'(x)$." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "First, we write\n\n$$\nf(x) = (\\sin{x})^3\n$$\n\nNow, we see that $f(x)$ can be expressed as the composite function\n\n$$\nf = u^3, \\qquad u=\\sin x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d f}{\\textrm d u} = 3u^2, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\cos{x}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{\\prime }(x) &= \\frac{df}{du} \\cdot \\frac{du}{dx} \\\\\n&= 3u^{2} \\cdot (\\cos x) \\\\\n&= 3(\\sin x)^{2}\\cos x \\\\\n&= 3\\sin^{2} x\\cos x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064042 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a483e892-90f2-51f4-80cd-2b1200cd0c37" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Composition of Trigonometric Functions Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4ebd0289-b278-5352-b7bd-10ae218c43fb" :question/math-academy-id "e-735" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $y = \\tan{\\left(\\sin(x)\\right)}$." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny = \\tan u, \\qquad u = \\sin x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d u} = \\sec^2 u,\\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm d x} = \\cos x\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{dy}{du} \\cdot \\frac{du}{dx} \\\\\n&= \\sec^{2} u \\cdot \\cos x \\\\\n&= \\sec^{2} (\\sin x)\\cos x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a483e892-90f2-51f4-80cd-2b1200cd0c37" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Composition of Trigonometric Functions Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab496644-0eea-5183-a453-56693656c987" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\cos x\\sin (\\cos x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063006} {:answer/id #uuid "af5114a0-ffc1-5411-bb8f-c0d496caf27b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\cos x\\cos (\\sin x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063007} {:answer/id #uuid "c71e2405-337a-57ba-87b2-17386379688e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sin x\\cos (\\cos x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063008} {:answer/id #uuid "eb27c530-bb19-5883-b23d-768448bf54ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sin x\\cos (\\sin x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063009} {:answer/id #uuid "45bc7f9f-8d02-50ed-9a1f-42e81aa8fd39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sin x\\sin (\\cos x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c71e2405-337a-57ba-87b2-17386379688e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sin x\\cos (\\cos x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063008} :answer-field/id #uuid "388f85b8-8e2a-5fe4-abe4-21648326a68c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063005}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "55ba3ddf-3b81-51ce-a46b-d6facbbbea67" :question/math-academy-id "q-48643" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $y = \\sin (\\cos x)$." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "The outer function is sine and the inner function is $u=\\cos x$. Hence\n$$y'=\\cos(u)u'=\\cos(\\cos x)(-\\sin x)=-\\sin x\\cos(\\cos x).$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064858 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ec11481-cea2-514b-aa78-707fcf8838cc" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Power of a Trigonometric Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "957fe26b-ac75-54a9-9e2a-0ec7f3a0d2bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9\\sin x\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063659} {:answer/id #uuid "f4cac8b6-1af2-5e7c-8d04-169a5d6502d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\sin x\\cos^{2} x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063660} {:answer/id #uuid "17ddd4cf-50b0-5098-9504-054608cbc91d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063661} {:answer/id #uuid "451f68f1-197c-595e-9429-385e13e286b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9\\cos^{2} x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063662} {:answer/id #uuid "775ccd6a-dabd-591a-90a8-b4db265276aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\sin x\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "775ccd6a-dabd-591a-90a8-b4db265276aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\sin x\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063663} :answer-field/id #uuid "4059c0e9-ff43-5297-92ae-c3a09f60138d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063658}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "270b54b6-fdc6-5a75-af7c-f8052eee38ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-72154" :question/problem "Find $f^{\\prime }(x)$ when $f(x) = 9\\sin^{2} (x)$." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Write $f(x)=9(\\sin x)^2$. The chain rule gives\n$$f'(x)=9\\cdot2\\sin x\\cdot\\cos x=18\\sin x\\cos x.$$"}]}
